We are using the Option 3 API-based constants setup, called constantsAPI-sync. In this setup, the Django backend has a file named constants.py that stores all default messages such as ERRORS, INFORMATION, and VALIDATION. These constants are exposed through an endpoint /api/constants/ using a ConstantsAPIView class. On the React frontend, we use a MessagesContext that fetches these constants once via Axios and provides them globally to all components. Instead of hardcoding texts like “Email already exists,” we access them dynamically using their codes — for example, ERRORS["ES003"]. This approach ensures backend and frontend messages stay automatically synchronized and consistent without manual duplication.
